{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"StringChunk","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"String chunks are used to store groups of strings. Memory is"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"allocated in blocks, and as strings are added to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GStringChunk"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they are copied into the next free position in a block. When a block","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is full a new block is allocated.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When storing a large number of strings, string chunks are more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"efficient than using [func","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.strdup"},{"type":"text","text":"] since fewer calls to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"malloc()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"are needed, and less memory is wasted in memory allocation overheads.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By adding strings with [method","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.StringChunk.insert_const"},{"type":"text","text":"] it is also"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"possible to remove duplicates."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To create a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GStringChunk"},{"type":"text","text":" use [func"},{"code":"GLib.StringChunk.new","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To add strings to a "},{"code":"GStringChunk","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" use [method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.StringChunk.insert"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To add strings to a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GStringChunk"},{"type":"text","text":", but without duplicating strings"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"which are already in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GStringChunk"},{"type":"text","text":", use [method"},{"code":"GLib.StringChunk.insert_const","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To free the entire "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GStringChunk"},{"text":" use [method","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.StringChunk.free"},{"text":"].","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"It is not possible to free individual strings.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StringChunk","type":"reference"},{"text":" type acts as an owner of an underlying ","type":"text"},{"code":"GStringChunk","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"It provides the methods that can operate on this data type through "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StringChunkProtocol","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" conformance."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StringChunk"},{"type":"text","text":" as a strong reference or owner of a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GStringChunk"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StringChunkRef","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (instead of ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\